		summary = "**Shen Kuo** or **Shen Gua**, [[Courtesy name|courtesy name]] **Cunzhong** and [[Art name|pseudonym]] **Mengqi** (now usually given as **Mengxi**) **Weng**, was a Chinese [[Polymath|polymath]], scientist, and statesman of the [[Song dynasty|Northern Song dynasty]]. Shen was a master in many fields of study including mathematics, optics, and horology. In his career as a civil servant, he became a finance minister, governmental state inspector, head official for the Bureau of Astronomy in the Song court, Assistant Minister of Imperial Hospitality, and also served as an academic chancellor. At court his political allegiance was to the Reformist faction known as the New Policies Group, headed by Chancellor Wang Anshi (1021–1085).",
