		summary = "**Theodoric** (or **Theoderic**) **the Great** (about 454 – 30 August 526), also called **the Amal**, was king of the [[Ostrogoths]] (471–526), and ruler of the Ostrogothic Kingdom of Italy between 493 and 526, [[Regent|regent]] of the [[Visigoths]] (511–526), and a patrician of the [[Byzantine Empire|Eastern Roman Empire]]. As ruler of the combined Gothic realms, Theodoric controlled an empire stretching from the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the [[Adriatic Sea]]. Though Theodoric himself only used the title 'king' (rex), some scholars characterize him as a [[Roman emperor|Western Roman emperor]] in all but name, since he ruled a large part of the former [[Western Roman Empire]].",
